      "quote": "A ground for rejection under section 43 exists where a trade mark to be used in relation to pharmaceuticals or veterinary substances consists of an INN stem, or contains a notified INN stem in a meaningful way, and use of the trade mark in respect of the goods covered by the specification are not restricted to substances indicated by the INN stem. A section 43 ground for rejection may be overcome by the applicant agreeing to a condition of registration limiting use of the trade mark to goods containing substances belonging to the relevant INN stem."
