  "answer": "Manual practice — TMM/Part29/5/5/5 suggests this endorsement:\n\n“It is a condition of registration that any use in respect of pharmaceuticals will be limited to such goods containing substances belonging to the pharmacological group designated by the International Non- Proprietary Name stem <stem>.”\n\nThis is not an automatic requirement whenever a mark contains an INN stem. The passage concerns marks for pharmaceuticals or veterinary substances that consist of an INN stem, or contain a notified INN stem meaningfully, where the specification does not restrict the goods to substances indicated by that stem. The Manual says the applicant’s agreement to this condition may overcome the section 43 ground for rejection [TMM/Part29/5/5/5]. The quoted endorsement is Manual practice, not legislative wording."
